// Icelandic (is) — North Germanic (Insular), Latin script. Referee: wikipron isl_latn_broad (HUMAN, 10,093 headwords
// — LARGE, variants merged). `segmentJoin` strips the per-phone spaces. Icelandic has NO voicing contrast in stops —
// the contrast is ASPIRATION (pre- and post-), which is FOLDED in run 1 (the ʰ modifier + the neutralized ⟨b d g⟩/
// ⟨p t k⟩ → [p t k]); vowel LENGTH (ː, syllable-quantity) is folded (the Germanic call); DEVOICED SONORANTS (r̥ l̥ n̥,
// the combining ring) auto-strip in the backbone. Segments (vowels, the epenthetic-stop clusters ⟨ll⟩→tl etc., þ/ð,
// f→v/p) are compared directly. See docs/investigations/is_native_bringup_investigation.md.
